From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] PackageInstaller: an application somebody installs gets an icon

An application installed by opening its package in the file manager did not
appear on the home screen. It was installed, and it was in the list of all
applications, and until Launcher3 0014 nothing on the screen said that list was
there ("为什么微信读书还是不在首屏呢？", user, 2026-10-22, about the same
behaviour).

Launcher3 adds the icon for a session that says a person asked for the install:
SessionCommitReceiver.onReceive returns without queueing anything unless
SessionInfo.getInstallReason() is INSTALL_REASON_USER. AOSP's installer never
sets one, so every session it commits reports INSTALL_REASON_UNKNOWN, and no
application installed through it has ever been added to a home screen.
WeReadInstaller sets it (Installer.install), which is where this was found.

InstallInstalling is reached one way -- a person opened a package and confirmed
the dialog PackageInstallerActivity put up -- so the reason is not a guess
about the caller. An install that is not a person's goes through
PackageInstaller's own session API and sets its own reason; this activity is
not on that path.

diff --git a/src/com/android/packageinstaller/InstallInstalling.java b/src/com/android/packageinstaller/InstallInstalling.java
--- a/src/com/android/packageinstaller/InstallInstalling.java
+++ b/src/com/android/packageinstaller/InstallInstalling.java
@@ -125,6 +125,16 @@
             } else {
                 PackageInstaller.SessionParams params = new PackageInstaller.SessionParams(
                         PackageInstaller.SessionParams.MODE_FULL_INSTALL);
+                // PW3: who the install is for. This activity is reached one way -- a
+                // person opened a package and confirmed the dialog -- which is what
+                // INSTALL_REASON_USER names, and AOSP leaves it unset here
+                // (INSTALL_REASON_UNKNOWN). Launcher3 puts an icon on the home screen
+                // only for a session that says a person asked for it
+                // (SessionCommitReceiver.onReceive returns on any other reason), so an
+                // application installed from the file manager was reachable only
+                // through the list of all applications, with nothing saying that list
+                // is there (Launcher3 0014).
+                params.setInstallReason(PackageManager.INSTALL_REASON_USER);
                 params.referrerUri = getIntent().getParcelableExtra(Intent.EXTRA_REFERRER);
                 params.originatingUri = getIntent()
                         .getParcelableExtra(Intent.EXTRA_ORIGINATING_URI);
